This directory contains test profiles in separate directories, each
containing an input.par and input.str file. The models are described in
detail in the SuperLite methods paper (Wagle et al. 2023, ApJ 953 132).

The w7 smoke-test model (a typical SN Ia carbon-oxygen WD model from
Nomoto et al. 1984 at 10d from shock breakout) ships in the top-level
Input/ directory and is exercised by `make check` (Testsuite/first/test.sh),
which validates a run against the committed statistical reference ensemble
in tests/regression/reference/ (see tests/regression/ for the harness and
for how to regenerate references).

s18: A typical SN II-P model from Curtis et al. 2021 at 20d after shock breakout
SN 1999em-like: Another typical SN II-P model at 40d after shock breakout
A4: A typical SN II-n model at 5d, 10d, 20d, and 30d after maximum in bolometric
    luminosity (LTE and NLTE variants)
SN 2017hcc-like: A luminous SN II-n model at 35d after shock breakout

Note: the in_ndim values in the A4 decks were corrected to match their
input.str headers (the code refuses mismatched dimensions).
